</div>

<!-- MAIN WORKSPACE -->
<div class="main">

<!-- 1. LANDING PAGE -->
<div class="page active" id="page-landing">
  <!-- Official GeM 10th Year Celebratory Banner -->
  <div style="max-width:960px;margin:10px auto 20px;border-radius:6px;overflow:hidden;box-shadow:0 4px 14px rgba(0,51,102,.12);border:1px solid #B0C8E8;">
    <img src="/static/gem_banner.png" alt="GeM 10 Years - भरोसे और बदलाव का दशक" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block;">
  </div>

  <div style="text-align:center;padding:15px 20px 20px;">
    <h2 style="font-size:22px;color:var(--navy);margin-bottom:6px;">Welcome to SETU &mdash; Govt Innovation Trial Portal</h2>
    <p style="font-size:14px;color:var(--muted);margin-bottom:28px;">
      Govt departments can safely test new technology in real field conditions without open tenders &mdash; Under <strong>General Financial Rules (GFR) 2017 Rule 173</strong>
    </p>
    <div class="role-grid">
      <div class="role-card" onclick="showLoginPage('buyer')">
        <div class="role-icon">&#127963;</div>
        <div class="role-title">Govt Officer / Buyer Login</div>
        <div class="role-desc">Municipalities, Smart Cities &amp; Govt Offices looking to test innovative solutions on the ground</div>
      </div>
      <div class="role-card" onclick="showLoginPage('seller')">
        <div class="role-icon">&#127970;</div>
        <div class="role-title">Supplier / Seller Login</div>
        <div class="role-desc">DPIIT-recognized startups &amp; GeM verified sellers ready to demonstrate their products in real field trials</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p style="font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:14px;">
      Portal Administration &amp; Auditor Login: <a href="#" onclick="showLoginPage('admin')">Administrator Login &rarr;</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card" style="max-width:820px;margin:15px auto;border:1px solid #B0C8E8;">
    <div class="card-header" style="background:#003366;font-size:14px;">
      &#9878; How This Works: GFR 2017 Rule 173 (Govt Technology Trial Framework)
    </div>
    <div class="card-body" style="font-size:13px;color:#222;line-height:1.8;">
      Normally in government tenders, officers are forced to pick the lowest bidder (L1), even if their product fails. 
      Under <strong>GFR 2017 Rule 173</strong>, government departments have the legal power to bypass tenders and run <strong>safe, controlled field trials (Sandboxes)</strong> to test if innovative technology actually works before spending full public funds:
      <ul style="margin:10px 0 10px 22px;">
        <li><strong>Smart 4-Factor AI Matching:</strong> Govt officers state their civic problem (e.g. drain flood sensors or drone surveillance); AI instantly matches verified Indian startups and GeM sellers on technical capability.</li>
        <li><strong>Safe 3-Stage Trial Agreement (MoU):</strong> No advance loss! Budget is locked safely and paid step-by-step: <strong>20% Setup</strong>, <strong>50% Working Proof</strong> (must work in the field), and <strong>30% Final Handover</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>100% Vigilance &amp; CVC Protection:</strong> Every trial approval, sensor data proof, and payment release is locked in an unbreakable digital audit ledger with SHA-256 proof.</li>
        <li><strong>GeM Fast-Track Purchase Certificate:</strong> Once the product successfully passes the field trial, the seller gets an official certificate to sell directly to any government department in India on GeM without tenders!</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

